    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Born to a bear keeper of the Hippodrome and working as an actress in her youth, Theodora married Justinian after a law of 524 allowed senators to marry actresses, and was crowned empress in 527.</li><li>As empress she advised Justinian, steadied the court during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nika-riots">Nika riots</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a>'s account, closed brothels, sheltered persecuted Miaphysites against her husband's Chalcedonian policy, and plotted the fall of rivals such as John the Cappadocian.</li><li>Most of what is known of her comes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a>, who praised her in public and slandered her in his Secret History, and historians remain divided over how far to believe him.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Theodora sheltered so many persecuted Miaphysite monks in the palace that on one occasion several hundred gathered in a grand chamber and the floor collapsed.</p></aside>
    </section>

